<description>&lt;p&gt;President de la Espriella opened a Colombian embassy in Jerusalem, prompting condemnation from Pakistan and other Muslim states, and launched a cultural counterrevolution that includes removing more than thirty artworks from the National Museum. An acid-attack survivor cancelled a planned euthanasia after a public appeal, while a preacher was killed by members of a criminal group in Cartagena. A Colombian asylum seeker was tackled by ICE agents outside his home in Washington, and a video shows a Colombian asylum seeker being detained by ICE. The peace tribunal charged former FARC members with anti-Indigenous crimes, and 225 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hill&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxONXJPVTd0cHA0cmJ3cnFmWWN5SFl2dXlRa0x0Q2FsTWt5SDlnRkZvNG1MNlEwenJEWWJveVlBZkNZTlhUS3FIN3BIUzExd1c4c3JnUFI0dlVETk1qdENOVFNBZlpGRDZMSXFJWkp3alUyRnROSUJRSzU4bXBSQnBaUjBWd3ZQRXV0VThv?oc=5&quot;&gt;Jacobin&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Escudo Digital&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE1TTTkyVGppeko1WEFvMmEzamUxWU9rVzBaOEh6MklzRUhjRUVaWkJidHEweHFXTDcyT2dERWt4ZDV6bG9hSVdvVWtrTXpLcVRqZjhBVUVNZ2hqdkct?oc=5&quot;&gt;International Crisis Group&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Breitbart News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxOMHdqckFXeU5Pc0hXUmNvR0Q2LUx1Y29Mdkh0V2VpbUh0Y3MyR2NDb2t3UTRkVkoycU5yUTBQckllc1VGeHhyeFhsOWFxaVowd2FvakVHS3V1WFFIQjR5TUxISTVfRXQ2M29vN1F0ME1qektaZFFBZVVlN2FKQUdHMFdEY2xyWHdBUXo5UjV6cjlwZmpmMk9VV3Q5c0oyT192MV92UU5n?oc=5&quot;&gt;ColombiaOne.com&lt;/a&gt;, &